{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"code","value":"const RunDetachedCapability: Capability<true, \"run-detached\">;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts#L361","children":[{"type":"text","value":"packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts:361"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Whether this run's teardown DID detach — the disconnect was survived, the\nagent is still working, and a later attach can take the run over."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The past-tense counterpart of "},{"type":"link","href":"DetachableRunCapability.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"DetachableRunCapability"}]},{"type":"text","value":", and the two must\nnot be confused:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"detachABLE"}]},{"type":"text","value":" is published at "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"setup"},{"type":"text","value":", and only says a disconnect "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"may"}]},{"type":"text","value":" be\nsurvived (a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"RunStore"},{"type":"text","value":" and a durable log are wired)."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"detachED"}]},{"type":"text","value":" is published on the ABORT path, by the middleware that actually\nmakes the call — "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"withSandbox"},{"type":"text","value":"'s "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onAbort"},{"type":"text","value":", which is the only actor that has\nresolved BOTH out-of-band cancel bands ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"AbortInfo.cancelRequested"},{"type":"text","value":" and\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"wasCancelRequested"},{"type":"text","value":" on the record) and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"detachOnDisconnect"},{"type":"text","value":". An explicit\ncancel, a non-detachable disconnect, an error, and a normal finish all leave\nit unpublished."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Its consumer is the durable DELIVERY sink in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"stream-to-response.ts"},{"type":"text","value":": a\ndetached run's log must stay OPEN and un-terminalized so the takeover can\ncontinue it (see "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"wasRunDetached"},{"type":"text","value":" in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"../../../delivery-detach"},{"type":"text","value":"). Reading it\nis safe and race-free only because a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"for await"},{"type":"text","value":" over the chat stream awaits\nthe generator's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"return()"},{"type":"text","value":" — and therefore the whole "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onAbort"},{"type":"text","value":" chain — before\nthe sink's own "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"finally"},{"type":"text","value":" runs."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Read with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ optional: true }"},{"type":"text","value":": absent means \"not detached\", which is every\nother exit path and every app that has not wired durability."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Typed "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"true"},{"type":"text","value":", not "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"boolean"},{"type":"text","value":", for the same reason as\n"},{"type":"link","href":"DetachableRunCapability.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"DetachableRunCapability"}]},{"type":"text","value":": absence is the only negative, so publishing\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"false"},{"type":"text","value":" must not be representable."}]}],"headings":[]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n```ts\nconst RunDetachedCapability: Capability<true, \"run-detached\">;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts:361](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts#L361)\n\nWhether this run's teardown DID detach — the disconnect was survived, the\nagent is still working, and a later attach can take the run over.\n\nThe past-tense counterpart of [DetachableRunCapability](DetachableRunCapability.md), and the two must\nnot be confused:\n\n- **detachABLE** is published at `setup`, and only says a disconnect *may* be\n  survived (a `RunStore` and a durable log are wired).\n- **detachED** is published on the ABORT path, by the middleware that actually\n  makes the call — `withSandbox`'s `onAbort`, which is the only actor that has\n  resolved BOTH out-of-band cancel bands (`AbortInfo.cancelRequested` and\n  `wasCancelRequested` on the record) and `detachOnDisconnect`. An explicit\n  cancel, a non-detachable disconnect, an error, and a normal finish all leave\n  it unpublished.\n\nIts consumer is the durable DELIVERY sink in `stream-to-response.ts`: a\ndetached run's log must stay OPEN and un-terminalized so the takeover can\ncontinue it (see `wasRunDetached` in `../../../delivery-detach`). Reading it\nis safe and race-free only because a `for await` over the chat stream awaits\nthe generator's `return()` — and therefore the whole `onAbort` chain — before\nthe sink's own `finally` runs.\n\nRead with `{ optional: true }`: absent means \"not detached\", which is every\nother exit path and every app that has not wired durability.\n\nTyped `true`, not `boolean`, for the same reason as\n[DetachableRunCapability](DetachableRunCapability.md): absence is the only negative, so publishing\n`false` must not be representable.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: RunDetachedCapability\ntitle: RunDetachedCapability\n---\n\n```ts\nconst RunDetachedCapability: Capability<true, \"run-detached\">;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts:361](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts#L361)\n\nWhether this run's teardown DID detach — the disconnect was survived, the\nagent is still working, and a later attach can take the run over.\n\nThe past-tense counterpart of [DetachableRunCapability](DetachableRunCapability.md), and the two must\nnot be confused:\n\n- **detachABLE** is published at `setup`, and only says a disconnect *may* be\n  survived (a `RunStore` and a durable log are wired).\n- **detachED** is published on the ABORT path, by the middleware that actually\n  makes the call — `withSandbox`'s `onAbort`, which is the only actor that has\n  resolved BOTH out-of-band cancel bands (`AbortInfo.cancelRequested` and\n  `wasCancelRequested` on the record) and `detachOnDisconnect`. An explicit\n  cancel, a non-detachable disconnect, an error, and a normal finish all leave\n  it unpublished.\n\nIts consumer is the durable DELIVERY sink in `stream-to-response.ts`: a\ndetached run's log must stay OPEN and un-terminalized so the takeover can\ncontinue it (see `wasRunDetached` in `../../../delivery-detach`). Reading it\nis safe and race-free only because a `for await` over the chat stream awaits\nthe generator's `return()` — and therefore the whole `onAbort` chain — before\nthe sink's own `finally` runs.\n\nRead with `{ optional: true }`: absent means \"not detached\", which is every\nother exit path and every app that has not wired durability.\n\nTyped `true`, not `boolean`, for the same reason as\n[DetachableRunCapability](DetachableRunCapability.md): absence is the only negative, so publishing\n`false` must not be representable.\n"}
